  "method": "Tag groups proposed after a look at the object motion and the robot contacts of all 32 runs. Each value is assigned by the rule of its group from numbers of the recorded episode. Film strips of 5 runs were inspected; they agree with the tags (objects that lie on their side in the tipped runs). No program text was read.",
  "rules": "experiments/contacts/tag_rules/rearrange3d.py"
 },
 "insights": [
  "20 runs lift each object (pick and place), and 11 runs slide the objects on the shelf. No distance sees this difference well (0.60 and 0.61).",
  "All opus5-source, astra and astra-source runs lift.",
  "25 of 32 runs move the boxed drink first.",
  "The contact view sees the hold, the end pose and the side effects (about 0.9). Two of these three tag groups come from the contacts."
 ],
